          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zǐsè is built from zǐ 'purple' and sè 'colour', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tsjeX and srik (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first as a colour between the pure ones."
            }
          ]
        },
